/P 228 0 R
/E (In Underwater Optical Communication \(UWOC\), turbidity \(NTU\) causes attenuation and scattering of optical signals. This changes the received signal strength, making fixed-threshold detection unreliable. The objective is to use supervised machine learning to classify transmitted bits \(0 or 1\) accurately under varying turbidity conditions.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [5]
>>
